### Parsing an invalid SVCB or HTTPS RR can panic in golang.org/x/net/dns/dnsmessage
BIT-golang-2026-46600 / [CVE-2026-46600](<a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46600" data-markdown-generated-content="">https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46600</a>) / [GO-2026-5942](<a href="https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5942" data-markdown-generated-content="">https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5942</a>)

&lt;details&gt;
&lt;summary&gt;More information&lt;/summary&gt;

#### Details
Parsing an invalid SVCB or HTTPS RR can panic when the size of a parameter value overflows the message buffer.

#### Severity
Unknown

#### References
- [<a href="https://go.dev/cl/786345" data-markdown-generated-content="">https://go.dev/cl/786345</a>](<a href="https://go.dev/cl/786345" data-markdown-generated-content="">https://go.dev/cl/786345</a>)
