							<span class="commit-summary " title="chore(deps): update all dependencies to latest (#212)">
								<span class="title-full-link-hover"><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/a998cc33899ea5fba1869a54e092ba4492250fea" class="muted title-full-link">chore(deps): update all dependencies to latest (</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/issues/212" data-markdown-generated-content="" class="ref-issue">#212</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/a998cc33899ea5fba1869a54e092ba4492250fea" class="muted title-full-link">)</a></span>
							</span>
						
						</span>
						
						<button type="button" class="ui button ellipsis-button" aria-expanded="false" data-global-click="onRepoEllipsisButtonClick">...</button>
						
						

						
						<pre class="commit-body tw-hidden">Bumps all direct dependencies to their latest versions.

| Dependency                    | From    | To           |
| ----------------------------- | ------- | ------------ |
| `gitea.dev/sdk`               | v1.0.1  | v1.2.0       |
| `github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go` | v0.45.0 | v0.56.0      |
| `go.uber.org/zap`             | v1.27.1 | v1.28.0      |
| `go.uber.org/zap/exp`         | —       | v0.3.0 (new) |

### Required code change
mcp-go v0.56 moved transport logging to `log/slog` and renamed the streamable-HTTP logger option to `WithStreamableHTTPLogger(*slog.Logger)`. Added a `log.Slog()` bridge (via the official `zapslog` adapter) so the HTTP transport keeps logging through the existing zap pipeline, and switched `operation.go` to the new option.

---------

