					<td class="message">
						<span class="message-wrapper">
						
							
							<span class="commit-summary " title="fix(milestone): persist `due_on` on create and edit (#189)">
								<span class="title-full-link-hover"><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/a77b54acdd87995b3e24f1271b89617cd58d86be" class="muted title-full-link">fix(milestone): persist <code class="inline-code-block">due_on</code> on create and edit (</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/issues/189" data-markdown-generated-content="" class="ref-issue">#189</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/a77b54acdd87995b3e24f1271b89617cd58d86be" class="muted title-full-link">)</a></span>
							</span>
						
						</span>
						
						<button type="button" class="ui button ellipsis-button" aria-expanded="false" data-global-click="onRepoEllipsisButtonClick">...</button>
						
						

						
						<pre class="commit-body tw-hidden">Fixes <a href="https://gitea.com/gitea/gitea-mcp/issues/187" data-markdown-generated-content="">https://gitea.com/gitea/gitea-mcp/issues/187</a>

The `due_on` argument was declared in the `milestone_write` schema but never read by `createMilestoneFn` or `editMilestoneFn`, so `opt.Deadline` was always nil and the field was silently dropped. This reuses the existing `params.GetOptionalTime` helper that already handles the analogous `deadline` field on issues and pull requests.

