					<td class="sha">
						
						
							
						
						<a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/9056a5ef27a06d0a22fc888da81e1807b700b0e7" class="ui label commit-id-short " rel="nofollow">9056a5ef27</a>
					</td>
					<td class="message">
						<span class="message-wrapper">
						
							
							<span class="commit-summary " title="Add `get_commit`, `get_repository_tree`, and `search_issues` tools (#162)">
								<span class="title-full-link-hover"><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/9056a5ef27a06d0a22fc888da81e1807b700b0e7" class="muted title-full-link">Add <code class="inline-code-block">get_commit</code>, <code class="inline-code-block">get_repository_tree</code>, and <code class="inline-code-block">search_issues</code> tools (</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/issues/162" data-markdown-generated-content="" class="ref-issue">#162</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/9056a5ef27a06d0a22fc888da81e1807b700b0e7" class="muted title-full-link">)</a></span>
							</span>
						
						</span>
						
						<button type="button" class="ui button ellipsis-button" aria-expanded="false" data-global-click="onRepoEllipsisButtonClick">...</button>
						
						

						
						<pre class="commit-body tw-hidden">Add three new read-only tools inspired by the GitHub MCP server:

- `get_commit`: Get details of a specific commit by SHA, branch, or tag
- `get_repository_tree`: Get the file tree of a repository with optional recursive traversal, pagination, and ref support
- `search_issues`: Search issues and pull requests across all accessible repositories with filters for state, type, labels, and owner

---------

