						<a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/1f7392305fe5b7aeaf84f245472b3b80f4593488" class="ui label commit-id-short " rel="nofollow">1f7392305f</a>
					</td>
					<td class="message">
						<span class="message-wrapper">
						
							
							<span class="commit-summary " title="docs: add `--scope user` to Claude Code examples in READMEs (#118)">
								<span class="title-full-link-hover"><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/1f7392305fe5b7aeaf84f245472b3b80f4593488" class="muted title-full-link">docs: add <code class="inline-code-block">--scope user</code> to Claude Code examples in READMEs (</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/issues/118" data-markdown-generated-content="" class="ref-issue">#118</a><a href="/gronod/gitea-mcp/commit/1f7392305fe5b7aeaf84f245472b3b80f4593488" class="muted title-full-link">)</a></span>
							</span>
						
						</span>
						
						<button type="button" class="ui button ellipsis-button" aria-expanded="false" data-global-click="onRepoEllipsisButtonClick">...</button>
						
						

						
						<pre class="commit-body tw-hidden">Small followup to <a href="https://gitea.com/gitea/gitea-mcp/pulls/117" data-markdown-generated-content="">https://gitea.com/gitea/gitea-mcp/pulls/117</a>. By using the user scope, the MCP server connection will be saved into the user&#39;s home directory, making it available for all repos, which is more useful than having to do this per-repo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 &lt;<a href="mailto:noreply@anthropic.com" data-markdown-generated-content="">noreply@anthropic.com</a>&gt;
